After XOR: a = 15, b = 27

Method 1 (arithmetic): a = a + b; b = a − b; a = a − b. It can overflow if a + b is larger than INT_MAX.
Method 2 (XOR): a ^= b; b ^= a; a ^= b. It never overflows, but both methods fail if a and b are the same variable (for example *p and *q pointing to one int), because the value becomes 0. In real code a temporary variable is clearer and just as fast.

